# CSVs are DATA, not text: store them byte-for-byte (-text disables all
# end-of-line conversion). data/raw/ is an immutable-snapshot store whose
# manifest.txt records a SHA-256 of the exact bytes written by the fetchers.
# With `text eol=lf` git rewrote CRLF -> LF in the blob, so the Linux CI
# checkout hashed to different bytes than the manifest recorded and every
# provenance gate failed there (btc/eth/xrp/sol/gold) while passing on Windows.
# Storing the bytes verbatim keeps the recorded hash a true content hash on
# every platform and honours the AGENTS.md rule-2 immutability guarantee.
*.csv -text
*.gemfile text eol=lf
Gemfile text eol=lf
*.pem text eol=lf
*.asc binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary